      "writtenOn": "2024-10-10T22:11:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`HAS_BINDER_SHELL_COMMAND` is only true if `binder_shell.h` is present. It is not in the NDK. What seems weird to me about this is that either:\n1. `binder_shell.h` is not needed for proper usage of binder, and we don\u0027t need `sys::AIBinder_Class_setHandleShellCommand(class, None)` to initialize it.\n2. `binder_shell.h` *is* needed for proper usage, and nobody using the NDK is fully initializing their binders.\n\nIf it\u0027s #1, I think we should just delete the `None` line. If it\u0027s #2, then we probably need a separate bug.",
      "parentUuid": "9b6ac912_85b74f1f",
      "revId": "4d0cdf00685d1e591716d39bbbd4dcbb8a6dee71",
